From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 05:06:10 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 084/207] In-model runner: straight-line integer cells run on
 the graph bank

A fence or REPL cell of assignments, q, r = divmod(x, y), ';' and prints of integer expressions or one
== / != runs as graph packets in turn: names expand to their definitions by text, so each print is literals
only, and x == y is bank arithmetic on x - y printed as True or False. This owns the whole-problem cell the
runner guide elicits (S1 d_mirror, big-number-019).
